  <h1>Boiler Advice for Woodthorpe Homeowners</h1>
  <p>Woodthorpe is one of the areas we're in and out of most weeks — it's just up the road from our base in Acomb, so when something goes wrong here we're rarely far away. This page pulls together the questions Woodthorpe homeowners actually ask us: what things cost, how to know you're dealing with a proper Gas Safe engineer, and what to do when the boiler picks the worst possible moment to give up.</p>

  <h2>How much does a new boiler cost in Woodthorpe?</h2>
  <p>Same as anywhere else in York — a like-for-like combi swap typically starts from £2,000, and a system-to-combi conversion (where more pipework is involved) starts from £3,000. Most jobs land somewhere in the £2,000–£3,000 range depending on the boiler, the property, and how much extra work the pipework needs. We quote for free, in writing, before anything is agreed — no pressure to take the biggest boiler on the van.</p>
  <p>See our <a href="/new-boiler-installation-woodthorpe/">New Boiler Installation in Woodthorpe</a> page for the full breakdown, or read our <a href="/advice-centre/new-boiler-cost/">honest guide to new boiler costs</a> for more detail on what drives the price up or down.</p>

  <h2>Finding a Gas Safe engineer in Woodthorpe</h2>
  <p>Always check any engineer's Gas Safe registration before they touch your boiler — it's a legal requirement, not a nice-to-have, and you can check anyone's number on the official Gas Safe Register. We're registered under 570248, and we're also Worcester Bosch and Ideal accredited, which matters if you want your manufacturer's warranty to actually mean something. A lot of the calls we get from Woodthorpe start with "I've been let down by someone else" — so if that's you, you're not the first, and it's an easy one to put right.</p>

  <h2>Boiler breakdowns — what to do first</h2>
  <p>If you've got no heating or hot water, check the pressure gauge first — anything below 1 bar usually points to a leak or a recent radiator bleed rather than something more serious. If the pressure's fine but nothing's working, an error code on the display (if there is one) will often tell us most of what we need to know before we even arrive. Either way, give us a call and tell us what you're seeing — it usually helps us get to you faster with the right parts.</p>
  <p>If it's an elderly parent or a vulnerable neighbour with no heating, say so when you call — those are the jobs we push to the top of the list, not the bottom.</p>
  <p>Our <a href="/boiler-repairs-woodthorpe/">Boiler Repairs &amp; Breakdowns in Woodthorpe</a> page has our current call-out pricing, and our <a href="/advice-centre/why-is-my-boiler-losing-pressure/">pressure troubleshooting guide</a> covers what you can safely check yourself first.</p>

  <h2>Don't wait for it to break — get it serviced</h2>
  <p>An annual service is £85 and it's the single easiest way to avoid an emergency callout in the first place — it also keeps your manufacturer's warranty valid, which most people don't realise lapses without one. If you're a landlord in Woodthorpe, this is also where your gas safety certificate (CP12) comes from — see our <a href="/gas-safety-landlords/">Gas Safety &amp; Landlords</a> page for what that covers.</p>
  <p>If you'd rather not think about it every year, our <a href="/boiler-care-plans/">Boiler Care Plans</a> start from £12.99/month and include your annual service, and a free CO alarm.</p>

  <h2>Book a Woodthorpe visit</h2>
  <p>Whether it's a quote for a new boiler, a repair, or your annual service, we cover Woodthorpe every week. Call us and tell us what's going on — we'll give you a straight answer, not a sales pitch.</p>
